% huey_dewey_louie: a Picat model from DCP Rosetta.
%
% Huey, Dewey and Louie are being questioned by their uncle, and each may be guilty or not. They make these
% statements, and as cub scouts they cannot tell a lie:
% - Huey: Dewey and Louie have an equal share in it; if one is guilty, so is the other.
% - Dewey: If Huey is guilty, then so am I.
% - Louie: Dewey and I are not both guilty.
%
%   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/huey_dewey_louie.html
% Save this model as model.pi and run it (Picat 3.9, https://picat-lang.org) with:
%   picat model.pi
import cp.

% The puzzle reads no data: the statements are fixed in the model. Each guilt is 1 (guilty) or 0 (not guilty).
model(_Data, Vars, Outputs, Options) =>
    [Huey, Dewey, Louie] :: 0..1,
    % Huey's statement is true: Dewey and Louie are both guilty or both not guilty
    Dewey #= Louie,
    % Dewey's statement is true: if Huey is guilty, then Dewey is guilty
    Huey #=> Dewey,
    % Louie's statement is true: Dewey and Louie are not both guilty
    #~ (Dewey #/\ Louie),
    Vars = [Huey, Dewey, Louie],
    Outputs = [huey = Huey, dewey = Dewey, louie = Louie],
    Options = [].

main =>
    model(new_map(), Vars, Outputs, Options),
    solve(Options, Vars),
    solve(vars(Outputs)),
    foreach(Name = Value in Outputs)
        printf("%w = %w\n", Name, Value)
    end.
